<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Merger plan favours Advance - analysts.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Merger plan favours Advance - analysts.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The A$2.65 billion merger proposal between Sydney-based regional banks Advance Bank Australia Ltd and St George Bank Ltd looks like favouring Advance Bank shareholders, analysts said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;My initial reaction is that it looks like Advance Bank shareholders are coming out of the deal quite well, whereas St George shareholders are coming out not so well,&quot; said one Sydney-based banking analyst.</p>
<p>Analysts said there was still a possibility that a major bank could come in and make a bid for either St George or Advance, but it looked unlikely at this stage.</p>
</text>
